# pap/.env.example — PAP environment configuration template
#
# SETUP (new node / fresh clone):
#   1. Copy this file:  cp pap/.env.example pap/.env
#   2. Edit pap/.env — fill in any values marked  ← CHANGE THIS
#   3. Bootstrap the database:  python pap/bootstrap.py
#   4. Start the service:       cd pap && uvicorn main:app --port 3002
#
# LAYERING: pap/.env wins over the root .env for any key defined in both.
# Provider API keys (Azure, AWS, etc.) belong in the ROOT .env, not here.
#
# NOTE: .env is gitignored — never commit it. This .env.example IS committed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Peer-service connections (ALL REQUIRED — no localhost fallback) ───────────
# PAP refuses to start if any of these is unset. SENTINEL_URL / COORDINATOR_URL
# are also declared below; keep them consistent.
POLICY_ENGINE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3003
GUARDRAIL_SERVICE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3001

# ── Database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SQLite (default): path is relative to the pap/ directory.
# The bootstrap script resolves this to an absolute path automatically.
PAP_DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///config/pap.db

# PostgreSQL (recommended for production or multi-node deployments):
# PAP_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg2://user:password@host:5432/pap_db
#
# With PostgreSQL you MUST run Alembic migrations instead of the bootstrap script:
#   cd pap && alembic upgrade head
#   python bootstrap.py    ← seed step still applies

# ── Rolling retention (metric snapshots + audit eval-trail) ───────────────────
# OFF by default. Under sustained traffic these grow unbounded; this prunes older
# rows in-process (SQLite only), keeping a rolling window in DAYS. Same feature
# runs locally and on Cloud Run.
#
# RECOMMENDED — bounds the bloat WITHOUT changing trust scores: prune ONLY the
# metric snapshots (the biggest, unbounded grower) and leave the audit trail
# intact. Per-agent trust scores are an ALL-TIME sum over audit rows, so pruning
# audit shifts them; metric snapshots have no score effect.
#   PAP_RETENTION_METRICS_DAYS=1   # metric_snapshots / trust_score_snapshots only
#   PAP_RETENTION_INTERVAL_MIN=60  # how often the sweep runs (minutes)
#
# Audit ceiling (safe insurance): per-agent trust scores are an ALL-TIME sum over
# audit rows. A 7-day cap prunes NOTHING until rows exceed 7 days — so on a fresh
# deploy (audit starts empty) it has NO effect during a <=7-day run, and only bounds
# a longer-running instance (scores then become a rolling 7-day window). Recommended
# alongside the metrics window above:
#   PAP_RETENTION_AUDIT_DAYS=7     # eval-trail ceiling; trims only rows older than 7d
# Prune BOTH buckets to the same short window only if you accept scores shifting:
#   PAP_RETENTION_DAYS=1           # master + default window for BOTH buckets

# ── Security ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Secret key for PAP session signing (Phase 3 auth). Change in production.
PAP_SECRET_KEY=change-me-in-production         # ← CHANGE THIS in production

# ── Network binding ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PAP_HOST=0.0.0.0
PAP_PORT=3002

# ── Dashboard service (dashboard_main.py on port 3003) ───────────────────────
# The Dashboard is a separate process sharing the same DB as the PAP.
# Start with: cd pap && uvicorn dashboard_main:app --port 3003
DASHBOARD_HOST=0.0.0.0
DASHBOARD_PORT=3003

# ── External service URLs (read by /v1/ui-config → dashboard.html) ────────────
# Override these if your Sentinel / Coordinator / Assurance services run
# on non-default ports.  Use 127.0.0.1, not localhost (avoids IPv6 stall on Windows).
ASSURANCE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3010
SENTINEL_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3012
COORDINATOR_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3013
